# This repository verifies bytes, so git must not rewrite them.
#
# The official data.gov.in tables and the registry export are recorded in _manifest.json with their
# sha256, and tests/test_data.py checks every file against it. The reference tables are asserted to
# rebuild byte-for-byte. Git's default line-ending conversion (core.autocrlf, on by default with Git
# for Windows) silently breaks all of that on clone: a CSV stored with LF is checked out with CRLF,
# its hash changes, and the test suite fails on a machine where nothing is actually wrong.
#
# -text disables that conversion for everything. What was committed is what you get, on every platform.
* -text

# Be explicit about the binaries as well, so no tool treats them as diffable text.
*.pdf    binary
*.xls    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.parquet binary
*.png    binary
*.svg    binary
*.geojson binary
